Z||000005||Formula88||06-09-2001||03:38 AM||||Not trying to flame anyone, but the threads about "will my car win this race?" are a bit silly.  Why bother racing if you already know who's gonna win?  If you want to find out, go race the person and find out.  Never under estimate driver skill, either.  Many a fast car has lost to a slower one because the driver screwed up.  Might get a good kill that way.  But at least you know - rather than relying on what other people say.  Besides, ask any ricer Honda owner and his car is faster than a Saturn 5 rocket.  Either put up or shut up, IMO.<P>Now lets get out there and have some fun, guys. (and girls!)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||13
Z||000006||danny boy||06-09-2001||03:51 AM|||| Cars I have beat with my 87GT auto:<P>every Honda product I have ever raced.<BR>Eclipse/Talon/Laser non turbo auto.<BR>3rd Gen Camaro firebird V6<BR>3rd gen Camaro firebird 305V8<BR>mid 80's Buick Century 2.8FWD<BR>2nd Gen Firebird 3.8 auto.<BR>Fox body mustangs (out ran on windy roads)<BR>Domino's Pizza Delivery truck<BR>Escort GT<BR>80s/early90s cavalier Z24<P>My car is stock except for cat removed and Jacobs ignition.<P>Cars I've lost to:<BR>RX7 turbo<BR>3000GT SL (non turbo)<BR>'86 SE 4 speed<BR>Dodge Caravan turbo<BR>'68 Camaro<BR>Ferrari 308<BR>'98 Vette<BR>Talon turbo AWD<P>   Go Figure<P><P>------------------<BR>don't push the A/c button.. it catches the car on fire      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PFF_sig_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||thomas_l||06-09-2001||10:08 AM||||My 87 GT will beat most ricers to the gas pumps.||||reg||6
